% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `as_event_handler`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: no body of it
% is printed or held.  MENDELS (IFS No.61, psi/mendels.py, 2026-11-27).
% MINIMAL: the handler MENDELS's ESP device names in its catcher list
% (esp_device.esp io/4: `:get_instance(#mendel_error, H, _)`, then
% `:refute_in(Process, [{#error, H, ""}], ...)`; error.esp's mendel_error
% has this nature and defines invoke/5).
%
% USAGE: docs/simpos/subsystems/shell.md §2.10 (as_event_handler: a
% handler class defines `:invoke(H, Event, Info, _, _)`; kappa2
% HLCMNG.ESP:29, 412-416 make one with new/2).

class as_event_handler has

% :get_instance(#C, H, _) -- INTERPOLATED from MENDELS esp_device.esp:19
% (the handler given to refute_in/5); the third argument is not used by
% the caller.  The body OURS: a new instance of the class each time
% (whether SIMPOS keeps one per class is not known).
:get_instance(Class, H, _) :- :new(Class, H);

end.
